<h2>Frozen squid and cuttlefish from India</h2>
<p>India's west and south coasts — Gujarat, Maharashtra, Kerala and Tamil Nadu — support a substantial squid and cuttlefish fishery and processing industry, supplying both whole and value-added (cleaned, tube, ring) frozen product to international markets. We work with processors across this coastal belt, the same one that supplies our frozen shrimp export line.</p>

<h2>A distinctly Mediterranean-skewed market — with a data caveat</h2>
<p>The USA is India's single largest squid/cuttlefish market, but what stands out in the trade data is the strength of Southern European demand: Spain, Italy, France, Belgium and Greece collectively take a substantial share, reflecting how central cephalopods are to Mediterranean cuisine. Worth flagging honestly: the reported export total for this specific HS code line looks lower than India's known cephalopod trade would suggest, likely because some volume is captured under adjacent, closely related HS subheadings that have shifted across classification revisions. We treat the country ranking as a reliable signal of where demand concentrates, but we don't present the headline dollar total as India's complete squid/cuttlefish export figure — and you shouldn't take it that way from any source either.</p>

<h2>Seasonality and the fishing-ban window</h2>
<p>India enforces an annual fishing-ban period on the west coast, typically mid-April to early June, to protect breeding stock during spawning season. This is a conservation measure rather than an export restriction, but it does shape when fresh catch is available for processing — peak processing and shipping availability runs from August through March, with the ban period representing a natural seasonal gap that's worth planning around for continuity of supply.</p>

<h2>How should I specify squid or cuttlefish?</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Form.</strong> Whole round, cleaned, tubes, rings or tentacles — each suits different end uses.</li>
  <li><strong>Freezing method.</strong> IQF for retail-ready product, block-frozen for foodservice/bulk buyers.</li>
  <li><strong>Size grading.</strong> Expressed as count per kilogram — this varies by market convention, so confirm your target grade explicitly.</li>
</ul>

